  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-plugin-leaderboard",
      "text": "[English](#install) | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\nCommunity plugin leaderboard for [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness). It reads the public GitHub topic [`dsh-plugin`](https://github.com/topics/dsh-plugin) and shows three boards **inside the Web UI**:"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-plugin-leaderboard",
      "text": "| Board | Meaning |\n| --- | --- |\n| **最热 / Hottest** | Most GitHub stars |\n| **最新 / Newest** | Most recently created |\n| **最火 Top 10 / On fire** | Top 10 by star density with a recency boost |\n| **推荐 / Picks** | Curated list stored in MySQL |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add github:shaoxia20240902/dsh-plugin-leaderboard\n```\n\nOr from a local checkout:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add /path/to/dsh-plugin-leaderboard\n```\n\nRestart `dsh web`. The sidebar foot shows **插件榜**. You can also type `/leaderboard` in a session, or ask the agent to show the hottest / newest / on-fire plugins."
    },
    {
      "section": "What you get",
      "text": "- **Sidebar panel** — three tabs, star/fork counts, copy-install, **copy an interpret prompt**, open the repo.\n- **Interpret prompt** — paste it into the Harness composer. The agent clones the repo and explains it in plain language: what it is, what pain it removes, what you see after install, how to start, who should skip it.\n- **Slash command** `/leaderboard [hot|new|fire]`.\n- **Tool** `list_dsh_plugin_leaderboard` so the agent can answer ranking questions.\n- **HTTP** `GET /dsh-plugin-leaderboard` on the host (used by the panel)."
    },
    {
      "section": "What you get",
      "text": "These repositories are third-party code. Review the source and pin a commit (`github:owner/repo#<sha>`) before you install one.\n\nBoards load first from the hosted API `http://101.34.27.122:3091` (MySQL), then fall back to GitHub. The recommend list lives only in that database."
    },
    {
      "section": "When GitHub is blocked",
      "text": "Default `access: auto`: try `api.github.com` first, then public HTTPS proxies (for example `ghfast.top`)."
    },
    {
      "section": "When GitHub is blocked",
      "text": "- **Board data** — the host retries through a proxy so the sidebar still fills in.\n- **Open repository** — official `https://github.com/owner/repo`. Host-swap sites such as kkgithub.com 404 on most repos, so they are not used.\n- **Details** — a page on the hosted API (`/r/owner/repo`) with description plus a working clone-via-proxy command.\n- **Copy install / Explain** — include a “clone via proxy, then `dsh plugin add <dir>`” command."
    },
    {
      "section": "When GitHub is blocked",
      "text": "**A GitHub token is sent only to the official API, never through a public proxy.** Public mirrors are third-party and can vanish; override them when you have a stable one:\n\n```yaml\n- id: dsh-plugin-leaderboard\n  config:\n    access: auto\n    githubApiBase: https://your-proxy.example/https://api.github.com"
    },
    {
      "section": "Ranking",
      "text": "- **Hottest** — `ln(1+stars) + 0.55 ln(1+forks) + 0.6×freshness + 0.4×DSH relevance − stale penalty`.\n- **Newest** — recency of creation raised to 1.8, times a traction term so empty shells lose to same-week repos that already have stars.\n- **On fire** — HN-style gravity `(stars + 0.65 forks) / (age+2)^1.55`, times recent motion. Top 10.\n- **Picks** — curated in MySQL."
    },
    {
      "section": "Ranking",
      "text": "The catalog merges a few GitHub search pages (stars + recently updated), then drops `deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness`, forks, and archived repos. The hosted API stores that catalog in MySQL, refreshes it every 30 minutes, and serves the sidebar from the database. Opening the panel never waits on GitHub. A manual refresh asks the origin to sync under `GET_LOCK`; concurrent clicks join or keep the last snapshot. The host process also keeps a short in-memory copy (stale-while-revalidate)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "Optional `cordis.yml` / profile patch on the `dsh-plugin-leaderboard` row:\n\n```yaml\n- id: dsh-plugin-leaderboard\n  config:\n    githubToken: # or set GITHUB_TOKEN / GH_TOKEN\n    topic: dsh-plugin\n\nUnauthenticated GitHub search is enough for a personal install. A token raises the rate limit if you refresh often."
    },
    {
      "section": "Develop",
      "text": "```sh\npnpm install\npnpm test\npnpm build\n```\n\n`lib/` is the runtime. The client bundle is `lib/client.js` and loads through the Web GUI module table."
    },
    {
